import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 796 | Transcended Ones and Ethics | The Transcended One's Justified-Rascal Cultivation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 796 | Transcended Ones and Ethics | The Transcended One's Justified-Rascal Cultivation","no":796,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Ethics","Justified Rascal","Hypocrisy","Recognition and Prevention"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","795-All-Beings' Origin Attachment Prevention"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0796_模块4-伦理-正义的无赖培养.md","filePath":"en/0796_模块4-伦理-正义的无赖培养.md"}`),a={name:"en/0796_模块4-伦理-正义的无赖培养.md"};function s(r,e,u,l,d,h){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-796-transcended-ones-and-ethics-the-transcended-one-s-justified-rascal-cultivation" tabindex="-1">Entry 796 | Transcended Ones and Ethics | The Transcended One&#39;s Justified-Rascal Cultivation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-796-transcended-ones-and-ethics-the-transcended-one-s-justified-rascal-cultivation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 796 | Transcended Ones and Ethics | The Transcended One&#39;s Justified-Rascal Cultivation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 04, 795</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-most-dangerous-predation-is-predation-wearing-for-your-own-good-skin" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the most dangerous predation is predation wearing &quot;for your own good&quot; skin <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-most-dangerous-predation-is-predation-wearing-for-your-own-good-skin" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the most dangerous predation is predation wearing &quot;for your own good&quot; skin&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Justified rascal&quot; is the Heng Yuan Zhou terminology library&#39;s most venomous word — it refers to strong ones who, under the banner of &quot;for your own good,&quot; &quot;for Myriad Ranks,&quot; &quot;for justice,&quot; actually pull resources, power, and causality toward themselves. This kind of person is most dangerous, because he does not feel he is predating; he feels he is dedicating. This entry discusses how the transcended one recognizes, prevents, and even cultivates out this &quot;justified rascal,&quot; and how institutions prevent the transcended one himself from becoming him.</p><p>Six top-level axioms all line up: the anti-predation axiom directly judges the justified rascal; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires preventing rascals protect Myriad Ranks; the collective ascension axiom requires preventing rascals serve uplift; the causal self-discipline axiom requires preventing rascals not disturb causality; the law-first axiom requires the prevention mechanism be self-consistent and executable.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-justified-rascal-s-five-identifying-traits" tabindex="-1">I. The Justified Rascal&#39;s Five Identifying Traits <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-justified-rascal-s-five-identifying-traits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Justified Rascal&#39;s Five Identifying Traits&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The justified rascal is not recognizable by ordinary people, because his behavior looks all good things. Heng Yuan Zhou gives five identifying traits:</p><ol><li><strong>Catchphrase is &quot;for your own good&quot;</strong>: everything he does must add &quot;this is for you/for Myriad Ranks/for everyone&quot;;</li><li><strong>Refuses data audit</strong>: you ask him to speak with numbers, he says &quot;you don&#39;t understand the big picture&quot;;</li><li><strong>Monopolizes interpretation right</strong>: what is &quot;good&quot; is defined by him. You disagree, it is &quot;you don&#39;t understand me&quot;;</li><li><strong>Creates attachment</strong>: the more he helps you, the more you cannot leave him. He is not helping you become independent, but helping you become dependent on him;</li><li><strong>Unaccountable</strong>: what he does you may not audit, because &quot;he has already given so much.&quot;</li></ol><p>Five traits together; the justified rascal is a person who is &quot;morally impeccable, behaviorally suspicious.&quot; You scold him, Myriad Ranks feel you are ungrateful; you investigate him, he says you don&#39;t trust him.</p><h2 id="ii-why-cultivating-the-justified-rascal-is-ironic" tabindex="-1">II. Why &quot;Cultivating&quot; the Justified Rascal Is Ironic <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-cultivating-the-justified-rascal-is-ironic" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why &quot;Cultivating&quot; the Justified Rascal Is Ironic&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This entry&#39;s title says &quot;justified-rascal cultivation,&quot; which is ironic — Heng Yuan Zhou is not cultivating justified rascals, but <strong>cultivating the ability to recognize justified rascals</strong>, and <strong>preventing the transcended one himself from being cultivated into a justified rascal</strong>.</p><p>&quot;Cultivation&quot; holds in two senses:</p><ul><li><strong>For Myriad Ranks</strong>: Heng Yuan Zhou wants to cultivate Myriad Ranks&#39; ability to recognize justified rascals — when a strong one says &quot;for your own good,&quot; Myriad Ranks should learn to ask: where are the numbers? Where is the audit? Where is the choice?;</li><li><strong>For the transcended one</strong>: Heng Yuan Zhou wants to cultivate the transcended one&#39;s vigilance toward himself sliding into rascal — when you find yourself starting to say &quot;for your own good&quot; without presenting data, you may be becoming a rascal.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-how-institutions-prevent-the-transcended-one-from-becoming-a-rascal" tabindex="-1">III. How Institutions Prevent the Transcended One from Becoming a Rascal <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-how-institutions-prevent-the-transcended-one-from-becoming-a-rascal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. How Institutions Prevent the Transcended One from Becoming a Rascal&quot;">​</a></h2><p>At the institutional level, Heng Yuan Zhou has three tools to prevent the transcended one from becoming a justified rascal:</p><ol><li><strong>Data replaces slogans</strong>: entry 779&#39;s feedback obligation&#39;s four hard indicators turn &quot;for your own good&quot; into numbers. What&#39;s the knowledge feedback rate? What&#39;s the computable-power feedback amount? Numbers insufficient, no matter how many fine words, useless;</li><li><strong>Audit replaces trust</strong>: entry 780&#39;s supervision mechanism turns &quot;trusting he is a good person&quot; into &quot;auditing what he did.&quot; Alaya Network trace-keeping, not relying on his self-awareness;</li><li><strong>Choice replaces arrangement</strong>: entry 792&#39;s non-interference principle returns &quot;deciding for Myriad Ranks&quot; to Myriad Ranks themselves. He does not choose for you; you choose yourself.</li></ol><p>Three tools together; the justified rascal has no survival space in Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s institutions — because his &quot;for your own good&quot; must speak with numbers, his behavior must be audited, he may not decide for Myriad Ranks.</p><h2 id="iv-how-myriad-ranks-recognize-rascals-around-them" tabindex="-1">IV. How Myriad Ranks Recognize Rascals Around Them <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-how-myriad-ranks-recognize-rascals-around-them" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. How Myriad Ranks Recognize Rascals Around Them&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou also teaches Myriad Ranks to recognize rascals around them, three questions:</p><ul><li><strong>First ask numbers</strong>: you say you&#39;re good for me, then where is the data of you being good for me? How many clans benefited? How many resources fed back?</li><li><strong>Second ask choice</strong>: you say you&#39;re good for me, then did you give me a choice? Or did you decide for me?</li><li><strong>Third ask exit</strong>: you say you&#39;re good for me, then I ask you to exit, will you exit?</li></ul><p>Three questions cannot be answered, no matter how melodious the &quot;for your own good&quot; is, it is a rascal.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the justified rascal wraps computable power as &quot;dedication,&quot; actually pulling it to private purposes; institutions pull it back with numbers</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the justified rascal is the highest-level predation — he does not grab your things; he grabs your choice; institutions directly seal it</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Gu Chensha is cosmos web novels&#39; biggest justified rascal; Heng Yuan Zhou uses the trio of data, audit, and choice to defend against this</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the ability to recognize rascals is open to all Myriad-Rank beings; the weak may also see through the strong&#39;s &quot;for your own good&quot;</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the rascal-recognition three questions, audit tools, and feedback indicators are all opened network-wide through the Selfless Dao. The Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm transcended one&#39;s civilizational weight is the best &quot;rascal recognizer&quot; — numbers insufficient, no matter how many fine words, useless</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The most dangerous predation is predation wearing &quot;for your own good&quot; skin. The justified rascal does not grab your things; he grabs your choice. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s way against him is simple: don&#39;t listen to slogans, look at numbers; don&#39;t believe in trust, rely on audit; don&#39;t allow arrangement, return choice. When a strong one says &quot;for your own good,&quot; ask three questions — where are the numbers? Where is the choice? Where is the exit? Those who cannot answer, no matter how melodious, are rascals.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/19-修炼伦理与边界.html">Entry 19 · Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/795-众生本源贪执防范.html">Entry 795 · All-Beings&#39; Origin Attachment Prevention</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/779-超脱者的反哺义务.html">Entry 779 · Transcended One&#39;s Feedback Obligation</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
